WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.880 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
Which number is larger when most of the
digits match?

2
00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:06.060 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
Compare from the greatest place value, not
from the right.

3
00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.840 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
For whole numbers with no leading zeros,
more digits means

4
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.270 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
a larger number. If the lengths match,
compare one column

5
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:16.410 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
at a time. Compare four hundred and fifty
six thousand,

6
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.340 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
seven hundred and eighty two, with four
hundred and fifty

7
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.970 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
six thousand, seven hundred and twenty
eight.

8
00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.550 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
Their hundred thousands, ten thousands,
thousands and hundreds match.

9
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.670 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
We have not found a difference yet, so
keep moving

10
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.490 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
right. At the tens place, eight is greater
than two.

11
00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:35.860 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
Stop there. The first number is greater,
so four hundred

12
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.730 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
and fifty six thousand, seven hundred and
eighty two is

13
00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.520 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
greater than four hundred and fifty six
thousand, seven hundred

14
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.050 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
and twenty eight. The ones cannot overturn
that difference.

15
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.660 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now compare three hundred and nine
thousand, nine hundred and

16
00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.750 line:1% position:50% align:center size:90%
